    "Actual Rust cleanup checks last/status, writes old_cpu.prevpid7864, performs existing inlined release_thread and decrements accounting; subsequent debug reads use independent descriptor, with no last reads after release. The x86 instruction-cache flush is the existing no-op.",
    "Manual final-image schedule path: arch_switch_context callfe81a1a0, CURRENT runqueue unlockfe81a1b8, CURRENT saved IRQ restorefe81a1cd, oldCPU cleanupfe81a1e6. r13 retains oldCPU,r12 last,ecx0 debug,edx16 PS_EXITED. Corresponding source and production relocations agree.",
    "The two selected production C commands use -mno-sse; the actual full Rust crate disables vectorization and SSE/AVX features. Selected newly emitted helper bodies use GPR code plus explicitly reviewed state instructions. Unchanged compiler/allocator/formatter/IRQ ABI decisions reuse accepted predecessor. No whole-kernel C retirement claim.",
    "Guard exact source036ef99e proves owner receipt equality, retired=true/no unproven Docker CLI, lease absence, exact common/shared identities, fresh stopped exact CID/nonce/profile. Guard0/directjoin and root27:4 postjoin reacquisition agree with actual receipt2b961080 and guardac467972. Stopped container/common/shared remain retained and terminal cleanup is unaccepted.",
    "Independent manual expert binds actual switched control flow and all call arguments. The checker first selected a movabs address load of process_sched_irq_restore_bridge passed to preparation as a callback, not an IRQ-restore call. The real switched interval is linear: arch_switch_context, CURRENT runqueue unlock, CURRENT saved IRQ restore, oldCPU cleanup; oldCPU remains in callee-saved r13. Separate non-switch IRQ restore remains valid.",
    "Actual finite alignment probe checks production GCC14 SHA2092e32f and executes the real-header TU syntax-only with wait0/terminalExit0, noOOM, ccOK stdout and empty stderr. All ten exact sudo/Docker client records exit0 and are positively joined by accepted transport. Only newly created CID7eb020fe... is retired/removed with exact absence; old build CID/profile/mounts and both common/shared record inodes/hashes remain preserved. No image rebuild was needed."
  ],
